# Runtime dependencies — the direct ones, hand-written. Dev / test tools live
# in requirements-dev.in.
#
# This is an *input*, not something to install. `requirements.txt` beside it is
# the compiled lockfile: every package in the graph, transitive ones included,
# pinned to an exact version with a hash. Install that; edit this.
#
#     pip install -r requirements.txt          <- what CI and Docker do
#     uv pip compile ... (see requirements.txt header)   <- after editing this
#
# Transitive dependencies used to be deliberately unpinned here, on the
# reasoning that pip could resolve them and a shorter file is easier to read.
# The cost of that showed up on 2026-09-28: Starlette 1.7 changed
# `CORSMiddleware` to append `Vary: Origin` unconditionally, tests/test_etag.py
# was asserting the whole header string, and a push that touched only frontend
# code turned CI red. Nothing in this repository had changed. That is the
# failure mode a lockfile removes — upstream releases now arrive when somebody
# asks for them, by recompiling, rather than on the next `pip install`.

